('B', '**Schema therapy:** in a multicenter trial of 323 patients with avoidant, dependent, obsessive-compulsive, paranoid, histrionic, or narcissistic personality disorder, schema therapy (which targets long-standing core beliefs) led to recovery more often than usual care or another psychotherapy (Bamelis et al., 2014). NPD made up only part of the sample.'),
('B', '**Common elements:** reviews find that the treatments used for NPD share clear goals, attention to the treatment frame, building the alliance, and monitoring the therapist’s own reactions; longitudinal studies show patients can improve, though gradually (Weinberg & Ronningstam, 2022).'),
